lines=['# KND checkpoint append finding','', '**0 original rows CONFIRMED, 0 FAILED, 9 OPEN. Checkpoint/append leaf credit stays SUSPENDED; prior checkpoint restoration remains 3/12.**','',f'The fixed 64-weight writer has 116 distinct transitions, all at capacity1768. Budget90 permits at most45 positive/control pairs. {len(credited)}/45 selected pairs earn transition credit; {len(remaining)}/116 scheduled transitions remain uncredited. No timeout earns credit.','', '## Schedule theorem and scope','', '`KND_Schedule.exact_schedule` and `data_independent` prove the source-order metadata model is fixed. `append_count`, `final_length`, and `no_growth` establish116 appends,1768 bytes and no growth. [Schedule](KND_SCHEDULE.json), [frozen source excerpt](KND_writer.txt), [first compile and axioms](KND_L001/receipt.json).','', 'Layout: magic8, header8, proof/public/state/two roots32 each, four wide32, rho16,22 query words4,10 semantic scalars16, four z coordinates16, claim/rhs32, power16,64 weights16, checksum32. Weights span712..1736. Appended values do not control the fixed loops.','', 'The model is a manual source transcription, not an extracted Rust execution-equivalence proof. The1768 path requires variant final_len64 and weights.len64; arbitrary calls to the public checkpoint API do not have that guarantee. The writer reserves1768, whereas earlier arbitrary-prefix and checksum cuts use cap=len or cap1736 with growth to3472. Reachable lengths do not imply universally quantified arbitrary-prefix assertions. [Scope analysis](KND_SCOPE.md).','', '## Concrete transition evidence','', 'All twelve size32 and twenty-two size4 writer transitions were selected, followed by weight53..63. Each harness fixes len/cap/size, keeps initial/appended bytes arbitrary, and covers the entire live result (one arbitrary observed index for pairs1..33; every concrete index for pairs34..45). Constructor length/capacity and resulting prefix, appended bytes, length/capacity are asserted. Matched controls differ only by XOR1 of the expected byte; the name stays KND_transition. No copy stub was written. Exact KMX definitions are reused. KND_K071..K090 initialize through Vec::from(array1768) and concrete truncate; earlier attempts use with_capacity plus KMX prefix initialization. Array setup initializes spare bytes, so no additional uninitialized-spare refinement credit is inferred. [Constructor change](KND_CONSTRUCTOR_CHANGE.json). The observation change was made only for previously unrun transitions; KND_K066 was recovered read-only after its host process completed. [Change receipt](KND_OBSERVATION_CHANGE.json). New function-pointer/Option<fn> quarantine list: **empty**.','',f'Kani statuses: {dict(counts)}. Negative-control counterexamples are expected control results, not original-property failures. [Pairs](KND_PAIRS.json), [matching audit](KND_PAIR_AUDIT.json), [uncredited triples](KND_REMAINING_RUNTIME.json).','', '## Per-row decisions','', '| Original row | Decision and remaining obligation |','|---|---|']
for name,l in ledger.items():lines.append(f"| {name} | **OPEN.** {l['missing']} |")
lines+=['', 'Per-row positive/control receipt links: [KND_ROW_CREDITS.json](KND_ROW_CREDITS.json). Previous authoritative KMZ credits are retained.','', '## Lean composition and native corroboration','', '`KND_Composition.schedule_composition` composes transitions over the schedule with every runtime equality as an explicit premise. Thirty-eight focused chunks prove membership/capacity/byte laws for all116 entries; KND_partition proves their exact union. Nine row modules retain original byte projections and add conditional writer composition. These models do not discharge missing heap facts or widen reachability.','',f'Budget used: **Kani {len(kani)}/90, Lean {len(lean)}/50, optimized Rust {len(rust)}/5**. The focused generic module precedes chunks and dependent row bridges; the final manifest is imported once. Each top theorem has an axioms audit limited to propext, Classical.choice and Quot.sound. [Exact run metrics](KND_RUNS.json).','', 'Five optimized native runs check the116-step schedule,22 isolated query transitions,64 checksum payloads,64 selected weight lengths, and all finite original append-length domains. Every check includes a concrete XOR1 inequality. Native allocator witnesses do not replace symbolic Kani or function-oracle credit.','', '## Frozen scope and resource receipts','', 'Frozen Rust revision: `4bb3b3f51e16b4525f1d10336e2b0bcbbd775387`. Cargo.lock SHA256: `5782e6a32026fdd95d252d0db7ea20b16716e6deb4f5a397e744886bb6ba22ef`. KMX patch SHA256: `bcdf749b78eb6143789500d98d64ec3d407b8a17a6d1290c70c822473e8e9a67`. Exact stub SHA256: `c282a1272676cd56fd2702f60b17009bac9d252e495b1508459b01d6ed1cf9d9`.','', 'Each Rust/Kani invocation validates the reused scratch crate resolved graph against its copied frozen lock, sets CARGO_NET_OFFLINE=true and opt-level3, and checks the lock hash afterwards. Every admitted scope requires reservation allowed:true AND exit0, with MemoryHigh6G, MemoryMax8G, MemorySwapMax0, TasksMax64 and one own scope at a time.','',f"Maximum receipt RSS: {max(int(r['peak_rss_kib']) for r in runs)}KiB; reported swaps0 throughout. Exact targets, exits, wall times, RSS, swap, source revisions/hashes and axioms: [run index](KND_RUNS.json). [Admission audit](KND_ADMISSION_AUDIT.json), [transport](KMY_TRANSPORT.jsonl), [source archive](KND_SOURCE_ARCHIVE.json), [descriptive receipt-label errata](KND_RECEIPT_ERRATA.json).",'', 'No unchanged shape or final manifest was rerun. Persistent cache `/home/dombarker/project-offloads/codex-cx-kmy-cache-20261028` is retained. No crate/program file or wallet key/authority was changed, and no push occurred.']
final=next((r for r in lean if r['sources']==['KND_Final.lean']),None)
